---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Acquired"
  description="A personal museum for accessioning meaningful objects with photographs, provenance, catalog records, and the story of why each thing matters."
  ogType="article"
>
  <article class="kh-case section kh-case-acquired" data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="kh-case-head">
      <div>
        <p class="kh-case-kicker">06 / PRODUCT / ARCHIVE / COLLECTION SYSTEMS</p>
        <p class="kh-acquired-number">KH.2026.0006 / PERMANENT COLLECTION</p>
        <h1 class="kh-case-title kh-acquired-title">ACQUIRED</h1>
        <p class="kh-case-deck kh-acquired-deck">
          A personal museum for the things you keep — and why you kept them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <dl class="kh-case-meta kh-acquired-meta">
          <div>
            <dt>Role</dt>
            <dd>Concept / Product Design / Development</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Built</dt>
            <dd>2026</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Core idea</dt>
            <dd>Give meaningful objects a durable record for provenance and personal significance.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <div class="kh-case-actions">
          <a
            class="kh-pill kh-acquired-primary"
            href="https://iphiginea.github.io/acquired/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Open app ↗</a
          >
          <a
            class="kh-text-link kh-acquired-link"
            href="https://github.com/iphiginea/acquired"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="kh-case-body">
      <p class="kh-case-section-label">THE PROJECT</p>
      <div class="kh-case-prose kh-acquired-prose">
        <h2>Why I made it</h2>
        <p>
          We save photographs by the thousands, but the context around a physical object is much
          easier to lose: where it came from, who owned it, how it was acquired, and why anyone cared
          enough to keep it. I wanted a place for that information to live before it disappears.
        </p>

        <h2>What I built</h2>
        <p>
          Acquired is a personal museum for meaningful objects. Each object receives a permanent
          accession number and a structured record for its title, date, maker, classification,
          materials, place, acquisition history, provenance, and personal significance. Photographs
          can be uploaded and cropped for the collection, and each record can remain private or be
          made public individually.
        </p>

        <h2>The product logic</h2>
        <p>
          The system starts with accessioning rather than organizing. A collection code, year, and
          sequence number give every object a stable identity; the collection view makes those
          records searchable; and the individual object page keeps the full history behind the
          thumbnail. The structure is meant to remain useful as a collection grows instead of
          depending on folders, filenames, or memory.
        </p>

        <h2>Design direction</h2>
        <p>
          I borrowed the visual language of museum collection catalogs rather than social feeds:
          cream paper tones, archival red, brass accession numbers, serif display type, fine rules,
          and restrained object cards. The goal was to make documenting something feel like an act of
          preservation, not another post.
        </p>

        <h2>Built to keep growing</h2>
        <p>
          Supabase handles authentication, structured object records, and image storage. The app also
          supports image cropping and browser-based background removal, so object photography can stay
          visually consistent without changing the underlying record. The point is not to document
          everything you own. It is to preserve the things whose stories would otherwise disappear.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kh-case-next kh-acquired-next">
      <a href={withBase('/works/first-light/')}>
        <span class="kh-case-section-label">PREVIOUS PROJECT</span>
        <strong>← First Light</strong>
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .kh-case-acquired {
    --acq-red: #7b1420;
    --acq-red-deep: #5c0f18;
    --acq-cream: #f4f1e9;
    --acq-ink: #171717;
    --acq-brass: #a8874b;
  }

  .kh-case-acquired .kh-case-kicker {
    color: var(--acq-ink);
  }

  .kh-acquired-number {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    color: var(--acq-brass);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-acquired-title {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--acq-red);
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .kh-acquired-deck {
    max-width: 22ch;
    color: var(--acq-red-deep);
    font-weight: 520;
  }

  .kh-acquired-meta {
    border-color: rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.28);
    background: var(--acq-cream);
    color: var(--acq-ink);
  }

  .kh-acquired-meta dt {
    color: var(--acq-red);
  }

  .kh-acquired-primary {
    border-color: var(--acq-ink);
    background: var(--acq-ink);
    color: var(--acq-cream) !important;
  }

  .kh-acquired-primary:hover,
  .kh-acquired-primary:focus-visible {
    border-color: var(--acq-red);
    background: var(--acq-red);
  }

  .kh-acquired-link {
    color: var(--acq-ink);
  }

  .kh-acquired-prose h2 {
    color: var(--acq-red);
  }

  .kh-acquired-next {
    border: 1px solid rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.24);
    background: var(--acq-cream);
  }

  .kh-acquired-next a {
    color: var(--acq-red);
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .kh-acquired-title {
      font-size: clamp(4rem, 20vw, 6rem);
    }
  }
</style>
